UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Queen of Swords represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Discernment"—the high-frequency, mature phase of the air element where the sovereign consciousness has fully integrated its analytical capacity into a sharp, uncompromising, and elegantly detached presence. Moving beyond the knight’s kinetic momentum, the Queen signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Judge," where you no longer need to "charge" toward the truth, but instead command the clarity to see it instantly and hold it firmly. Visually depicted as a queen seated on a throne, holding a sword upright in one hand, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Precision"—the understanding that true power is the ability to maintain a field of mental purity, free from the entanglements of emotional sentiment or social pressure. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Integrated Intelligence," where your perceptions have stabilized into a consistent, piercing, and authoritative lens. When the Queen of Swords appears, your system is registering a "Maximum Clarity" status; you are secure in your judgment, and you are being invited to stop "explaining" yourself through defensive action and instead lead through the depth and truth of your insight. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your boundaries. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Honesty": honoring your own intellect, trusting the sharp edge of your perceptions, and refusing to blunt your truth to make others comfortable. To inhabit the Queen of Swords is to master the art of "Strategic Presence," recognizing that by simply owning your logic, your standards, and your analytical vitality, you are performing the most potent act of sovereign leadership possible—giving others the permission to face the facts of their own, internal realities.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Queen of Swords appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Cynicism," "Discourse-Collapse," or the catastrophic—yet instructive—failure to maintain your clarity, leading to a state of reactive, bitter, and often exclusionary volatility. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "being cold" or "judgmental" with "being objective," even as your internal operating system is experiencing a critical failure of its empathy-processing protocols. You are essentially "severing reality," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to "protect itself from disappointment" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually understand the complex, human reality of the situation. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "unbiased observer," while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of isolation, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of "performing toughness," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your clarity is a brittle, artificial projection. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of resentment"; you are obsessively trying to force people to see you as "above it all," refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, internal restoration of your authority is your own, deep-seated fear that without this performative armor, you would be seen as "vulnerable." The reversed Queen of Swords exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of irrelevance, and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense and sit quietly in the truth of your own, unvalidated state, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these performative, status-seeking scripts, perform a brutal audit of your internal sense of value, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize your soul-integrity over your social-standing. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical self-acceptance—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "being perceived as sharp" over the vulnerability of "being actually present," and realizing that until you are willing to let the performance collapse and stand in the raw, unadorned reality of your own, quiet truth, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom brilliance you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 41;
